'''Rei Ayanami (???)''' is a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]]. She was added in [[Version 8.7 Update#Update 8.7.5|Version 8.7.5]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 491
|rarity = SR
|name1 = Rei Ayanami (???)
|name2 = Awakened Ayanami
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Awakened Ayanami''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Use Awakened Ayanami as an anti-Dark tank similarly to [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]] or [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kotatsu Cat]], having 50% weaken, resistance and already high base health. She is irreplaceable in certain stages such as [[Refined Palate (Insane)|XP Megablitz!]] and [[Dark Premonition]]. Awakened Ayanami is incredibly effective against [[Director Kurosawah]] because she can tank many attacks from him, having potential to survive even longer depending on her weaken ability.

While you wouldn't normally use an anti-Dark tank because [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies have such high DPS, Awakened Ayanami has enough health to be one of the few usable (arguably fantastic) anti-Dark tanks. She can even make for a decent generalist early game thanks to her high health. In addition, her low-ish damage is better for stalling, though keep in mind that her range is extremely short when used for anything other than tanking.

{{Job|Classification = Tanker}}

